{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm","id":1403977,"title":"Ellie in VTM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-22T04:06:13-07:00","id":1403977,"title":"Ellie in VTM","content":"How doy think, who could be Ellie from Last of Us in VTM universe? A hunter? Last Daughter of Eve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T05:51:58-07:00","id":1403983,"title":"","content":"I'd say a dhampir,<br /> dhampirs can be imbued, so she could be a dhampir and hunter at the same time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:40:17-07:00","id":1403996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm#post1403977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How doy think, who could be Ellie from Last of Us in VTM universe? A hunter? Last Daughter of Eve?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it would really depend on what you want to do with her in the context of the game as if you wanted to, you could make her anything in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1403983#post1403983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a dhampir,<br /> dhampirs can be imbued, so she could be a dhampir and hunter at the same time</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, can I get a citation on that because I have never heard of that being a thing. Plus it does remind me of that splat-mixing min/maxing nonsense that WW created Samuel Haight to mock.<br /> <br /> Second, one doesn't need to be Imbued to be a hunter. There were hunters long, <i>long </i>before the Imbued became a thing. In fact, in V20 Hunters Hunted II, they actually bring up the Imbued at the end of the section where they take about other Supernaturals that hunters may encounter beyond vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T06:49:49-07:00","id":1404004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1403983#post1403983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a dhampir,<br /> dhampirs can be imbued, so she could be a dhampir and hunter at the same time</div> </div> </div> </div>From memory the rules exclude everything that is not pure mortal from being imbued. If I remember right even kinfolk and users of Numina are excluded. So how could a dhampire be imbued?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:25:46-07:00","id":1404017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1404004#post1404004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From memory the rules exclude everything that is not pure mortal from being imbued. If I remember right even kinfolk and users of Numina are excluded. So how could a dhampire be imbued?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see, well I just read it from the wiki,<br /> didn't check the source<br /> <br /> it's at the bottom<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dhampir_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dhampir_(VTM</a>)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1403996#post1403996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, can I get a citation on that because I have never heard of that being a thing. Plus it does remind me of that splat-mixing min/maxing nonsense that WW created Samuel Haight to mock.<br /> <br /> Second, one doesn't need to be Imbued to be a hunter. There were hunters long, <i>long </i>before the Imbued became a thing. In fact, in V20 Hunters Hunted II, they actually bring up the Imbued at the end of the section where they take about other Supernaturals that hunters may encounter beyond vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but the thing about Ellie is that she is immune to the zombie thing,<br /> I brought up imbued cause iirc they have some immunities to certain things like vampire curse<br /> <br /> if she was imbued, that could explain her immunity<br /> <br /> a non-imbued hunter could be immune with true faith, but Ellie doesn't seem the true faith type","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-22-2020, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:35:17-07:00","id":1404020,"title":"","content":"alright, I checked BJD, and dhampir can indeed be Imbued (page 144)<br /> <br /> which contradicts Time of Thin Blood which says they can't<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:54:24-07:00","id":1404034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1404020#post1404020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">alright, I checked BJD, and dhampir can indeed be Imbued (page 144)<br /> <br /> which contradicts Time of Thin Blood which says they can't</div> </div> </div> </div>This does surprise me, given every &quot;enemy&quot; book in the H:TR range has a box that states no one with a supernatural link etc can be in Imbued. Shame these is no sign of H20 to resolve this.<br /> <br /> Also guessing in part this goes down the line of each game line being separate, and not having to play by the rules of the others when only in house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T08:59:45-07:00","id":1404037,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I think she can be a dhampir with some special abilities (and, because of it, she can be Last Daughter of Eve as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","user":"trueann","date":". 07-22-2020, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T10:24:50-07:00","id":1404045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1404034#post1404034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also guessing in part this goes down the line of each game line being separate, and not having to play by the rules of the others when only in house.</div> </div> </div> </div>The more realistic reason maybe, many authorities of one line have limited knowledge about others<br /> <br /> M20 Gods and Monsters also says hunter can AWAKEN<br /> <br /> And Hunter Enemybook Spellbound says hunter is considered mortal when discussing Paradox, and they don\u2019t have avatars, which contradict each other<br /> <br /> So, this kind of limited understanding exists in all lines<br /> <br /> For me I will still use original stuff, only pure mortal (without any supernatural link) can become imbued","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-22-2020, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T18:25:34-07:00","id":1404143,"title":"","content":"As strange as it sounds, yeah it does appear that BJD has a rule that Dhampirs can become Imbued. It's not something I would use at my table but I can't deny that it's there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1404045#post1404045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more realistic reason maybe, many authorities of one line have limited knowledge about others<br /> <br /> M20 Gods and Monsters also says hunter can AWAKEN<br /> <br /> And Hunter Enemybook Spellbound says hunter is considered mortal when discussing Paradox, and they don\u2019t have avatars, which contradict each other<br /> <br /> So, this kind of limited understanding exists in all lines<br /> <br /> For me I will still use original stuff, only pure mortal (without any supernatural link) can become imbued</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page number on that as only thing I could find was a sidebar 'Night Folk Mages' and while it does mention 'hunters' it doesn't say anything about the the Imbued. In fact the only uses of the word 'imbued' is in regards to spells and magic items, not the Imbued themselves.<br /> <br /> Remember, while all Imbued are hunters, not all hunters are Imbued. Otherwise the Second Inquisition just got a lot scarier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T19:14:49-07:00","id":1404155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1404143#post1404143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As strange as it sounds, yeah it does appear that BJD has a rule that Dhampirs can become Imbued. It's not something I would use at my table but I can't deny that it's there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you have a page number on that as only thing I could find was a sidebar 'Night Folk Mages' and while it does mention 'hunters' it doesn't say anything about the the Imbued. In fact the only uses of the word 'imbued' is in regards to spells and magic items, not the Imbued themselves.<br /> <br /> Remember, while all Imbued are hunters, not all hunters are Imbued. Otherwise the Second Inquisition just got a lot scarier.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what I refer to<br /> <br /> You may think too much, that \u201chunter\u201d should refer to Hunter I think, it has used many times. Take a look at revised book of other lines, many use hunter instead of imbued<br /> <br /> And, I think make Dhampirs can be imbued is messy, breaking good rules have established","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T21:05:49-07:00","id":1404162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403977-ellie-in-vtm?p=1404155#post1404155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s what I refer to<br /> <br /> You may think too much, that \u201chunter\u201d should refer to Hunter I think, it has used many times. Take a look at revised book of other lines, many use hunter instead of imbued<br /> <br /> And, I think make Dhampirs can be imbued is messy, breaking good rules have established</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because there are many, many different hunter groups across the WoD but they are not Imbued. Hell, all of those groups, save for the Second Inquisition have existed for far longer than the Imbued have. Other game lines do not refer to the Imbued solely as 'hunters' for that reason because those lines have their own hunters.<br /> <br /> V20 Hunters Hunted II, the sequel to the original hunter book, long before HtR had even been conceived, brings up the Imbued but not as a hunter group among the others in the book, rather they are brought up with the other Supernaturals that VtM hunter might encounter alongside werewolves and mages and the like. Because Imbued Hunters are not normal hunters. All the Imbued are marked by an outside force and given powers that only their kind have. Normal hunters... well most of them don't have any supernatural power. For every True Faith wielding member of the Society of Leopold, there's dozens of hunters that don't have any powers.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Again</b></i></u>, all Imbued are Hunters but not all Hunters are Imbued.<br /> <br /> But if you truly believe you are right then as I said previously with the Dhampir thing, bring forth some citations and sources. Prove that they are indeed referring to Imbued Hunters rather than a blanket term for the various hunter groups out there. The M20 book you brought up does have hunters in it but none of them are Imbued so why would a sidebar in said book mean the Imbued when it says 'hunters' despite never actually bringing up the Imbued in it? Logically they wouldn't. If they wanted it to mean the Imbued, they would have either specifically said the Imbued and/or brought them up in the book. Nor is this a case like in HH2 where they present the information from an in-universe point of view that doesn't full know what the Imbued are, much less what they are called. They are presenting in a sidebar, intended for players and STs so there's not need to make things murky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T22:47:23-07:00","id":1404529,"title":"","content":"Funny thing, I'm blatantly ripping off MAFIA II right now for my present game. The players haven't played the game so I'm just adapting it to the Giovanni.<br /> <br /> The players think I've created an amazing ghoul chronicle and improved on Giovanni Chronicles IV.<br /> <br /> Haha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}